# Handler Chain Rules

- Handler ordering is behavior-critical and defined in `src/main/resources/spring/botConfig.xml`.
- The first matching handler processes update flow; avoid broad filters early in chain.
- If adding handler classes, ensure matching XML registration and dependency wiring.
- Validate command/filter overlap to prevent handler shadowing.

# Required Validation

- Verify affected commands with realistic update examples.
- Confirm unchanged handlers still trigger as expected after reordering.
